    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85040" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυ-μᾰθία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολῠμᾰθίη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>much learning,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. νόον ἔχειν οὐ διδάσκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heraclit.
					40
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυνοΐη,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Democr.
				65
			</span></i>, cf. Anaxarch.I, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				811a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				819a
			</span></i>; as a subject of competition, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Michel</u>
				913.8
			</span></i> (Teos, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πολύμνια.</span></div>
